### Prefix caching and the rolling snip

s15 caps a conversation at 50 messages. Once a run passes that, every lead call cuts the middle again and rewrites the archive marker. Everything after the first three messages moves position, so vLLM's prefix cache cannot reuse it, although that tail's content is unchanged. This is the edit that shift and EPIC can act on. Placeholder and summary compaction trigger only near the context limit, which the 50-message cap rarely lets a 128K window reach (table above).

| model | bench | lead calls after snip starts | prefix-cache hit before | after | share of re-prefilled tokens after |
|---|---|---|---|---|---|
| qwen3-32b | swe | 87% of 12955 | 67% | 30% | 93% |
| qwen3-32b | swepro | 90% of 19910 | 82% | 54% | 96% |
| qwen3-32b | tbench | 87% of 14345 | 61% | 49% | 86% |
| qwen3.8-27b | swe | 68% of 6138 | 79% | 12% | 93% |
| qwen3.8-27b | swepro | 60% of 4570 | 82% | 13% | 90% |
| qwen3.8-27b | tbench | 46% of 2906 | 86% | 9% | 89% |
| deepseek-v4-flash | swe | 60% of 4791 | 91% | 16% | 96% |
| deepseek-v4-flash | swepro | 65% of 5075 | 92% | 21% | 96% |
| deepseek-v4-flash | tbench | 33% of 2504 | 90% | 10% | 87% |
| minimax-m2.7 | swe | 70% of 6214 | 92% | 23% | 95% |
| minimax-m2.7 | swepro | 48% of 3368 | 88% | 19% | 85% |
| minimax-m2.7 | tbench | 55% of 3867 | 77% | 19% | 83% |

